     "description": "Since 2026-07-15 02:00 UTC the edge terminator is rejecting TLS handshakes for the customer-facing SNIs shop.meridian-retail.example, checkout.meridian-retail.example, account.meridian-retail.example, api.meridian-retail.example, catalog.meridian-retail.example, webhooks.meridian-retail.example with 'certificate has expired'. The presented leaf is the shared wildcard *.meridian-retail.example, whose validity ended 2026-07-15 02:00 UTC. The internal admin SNI (its own dedicated certificate) and the endpoints already moved to the current wildcard are NOT failing. Onset aligns with the certificate validity boundary, not a load-balancer or firewall change.",
